{#
  ==================== TWO SECTIONS CUT HERE, 2026-08-05 ====================

  "The rooms" (two captioned photographs) and "What Tajima runs" (a
  three-card brand-level block) were both added earlier the same day and both
  removed after review. Recording why, so neither gets rebuilt by reflex.

  "WHAT TAJIMA RUNS" TOLD THE SAME STORY TWICE, ONCE WELL AND ONCE FLATTENED.
  Traced sentence by sentence against the chapters above, its three cards
  carried two facts that were not already there ("most ramen shops buy both",
  and walk-in with no reservations) across nine sentences. One whole card,
  "One owner, since 2001", was chapters 03 and 04 compressed, running about
  four hundred words after they had already run in full.

  It also retold the beat that chapter 04 ends on and landed it somewhere
  weaker. Chapter 04 closes on "He didn't name it. He made it his.", which
  voice-tone.md calls the strongest line in the research file. The card closed
  on "Twenty-five years in San Diego, not twenty-five months", which is a
  comparative boast, and a third card ended on "produced by the floor, not by
  the marketing". Both break the rule the chapters are built on: every
  sentence is a fact, no sentence tells the reader what to think about the
  facts.

  Root cause worth remembering: the copy came from CLIENT_FACTS.md's "three
  tiers", which is an internal positioning framework for use "whenever the
  craft claim needs support". It reads fine as an argument and turns into
  brand-speak the moment it becomes a section of its own. It is a lens for
  writing page copy, not page copy.

  The one line that was doing work moved into chapter 06.

  "THE ROOMS" WAS DECORATION CHOSEN BY AVAILABILITY. It showed College
  Heights and Crown Point because those are the only two rooms with
  photography, not because either belongs to this story. College Heights
  appears nowhere in the narrative. Crown Point sat immediately after the
  Noodle Room chapter captioned "Crown Point, Opened 2025", so it read as a
  picture of the commissary, which it is not: it is the dining room. The
  heading, "Two of the six", announced the gap rather than showing the brand.

  DO NOT PUT AN IMAGE BACK ON THIS PAGE UNTIL THE REAL ONES EXIST. The three
  this page actually wants are Convoy, the founding room; the commissary; and
  Sam. None of the three is in the manifest. All three are in the photography
  ask drafted under SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md Open Decision #30, with #29 covering
  the wider gap. A page whose whole job is telling Sam's story should not run
  a photograph of a room he is never mentioned in.

  Structure is now: hero, chapters 01 to 06, quote pending, noodle band.
  =========================================================================== #}

